	"schema": "jpwb-sonar-rule-set/1",
	"$comment": "The rules the Sonar engine runs on JPWB (JAN-SONARCM D-1; roadmap S1). scripts/sonar/batch-runner.cjs asks the server for its defaults at each run (sonarlint/listAllRules) and sends it the differences: the rules here that are off by default, on; the defaults of these repositories that are not here, off; and the parameters below. It refuses a run whose server echo differs, and a rule the engine does not have. Editing this file changes what Sonar checks: a rule removed is a finding class no longer looked for, so it is a reviewed change, never a way to silence a finding (that is the exception register, D-5).",
	"basis": "On 2026-11-17 this list equals the rules SonarJS 14.4.0.46458 (SonarLint 6.3.0, language server 6.3.0.79979) turns on by default in these three repositories, as its server lists them (activeByDefault): Sonar way. So today the server is sent no difference.",
